    "summary": "High‑energy Greek Theatre set with standout Deal, Tennessee Jed and China>Rider",
    "blurb": "The May 22, 1982 Greek show bursts with tight playing from the opening Jack Straw through a rippin' Deal solo. Highlights include a soaring China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider jam, lazy lightning → Supplication segue, and an inspired Tennessee Jed performance. The Charlie Miller soundboard capture delivers crystal‑clear detail across the full set.",
    "review": "What unfolds at Berkeley's Greek Theatre is a quintessential early‑80s Dead outing—high voltage from the first note to the final U.S. Blues encore. Jerry Garcia rides a wave of inspiration, delivering what reviewers call \"the most rippin'\" Deal solo and an inventive Tennessee Jed narrative, while his guitar tone stays smoking throughout the night. Phil Lesh anchors the band with clear, punchy bass that shines in the jam‑heavy second set, especially on the seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition. Brent Mydland adds soulful texture on Never Trust A Woman and Good Times Blues, and his vocal reverb rounds out the mix. The rhythm duo of Bill Kreutzmann and Mickey Hart stays solid and tight, providing a steady foundation for the band’s exploratory flights, even as Bob Weir navigates a quirky intro to Man Smart, Woman Smarter before settling back into his usual groove. Across multiple recordings the show is praised for its high energy, flawless transitions, and especially the first‑set fire‑starter Jack Straw that sets the tone for an engaging two‑hour journey.",
